        "seo_questions": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "What covenant has Allah taken upon every believer (Momin) regarding patience and self-restraint according to Imam al-Sadiq (AS)?",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
        "summaries": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "This hadith from Imam Abu 'Abdillah (peace be upon him) describes a divine Covenant that Allah has imposed upon every true believer: that he will endure the trial of not being believed, will refrain from fully avenging himself against his enemies, and will find no comfort for his nafs except by holding it to account and exposing its faults. The concluding image of the Momin as 'harnessed' (muljam) conveys that restraint of the soul and its desires is the very hallmark of genuine faith.",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
